&lt;span class="section-tag"&gt;Portfolio&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;h2 class="section-title"&gt;Featured &lt;span&gt;Projects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="divider"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class="section-sub"&gt;Each project is a story — a question I had, a challenge I tackled, and an insight I uncovered.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="projects-list"&gt;

  &lt;!-- PROJECT 1: Bollywood --&gt;
  &lt;div class="project-card"&gt;
    &lt;div class="project-card-inner"&gt;
      &lt;div class="project-meta"&gt;
        &lt;span class="project-category"&gt;Data Analysis & Visualization&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;h3 class="project-title"&gt;Bollywood Movie Analysis: Where I Fell in Love with Data Science&lt;/h3&gt;
      &lt;p class="project-highlight"&gt;This project changed everything for me. As someone who loves Bollywood movies (especially Shah Rukh Khan!), I wanted to explore how data could tell stories about my favorite actors.&lt;/p&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;Key Questions I Explored&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;How does the genre of a movie influence its IMDB rating?&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;Are established actors linked to higher movie ratings over the years?&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;What I Discovered&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shahid Kapoor:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong recent performance with higher ratings in 2022–2023&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salman Khan:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluctuating ratings, suggesting mixed audience reception&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Akshay Kumar & Ajay Devgn:&lt;/strong&gt; Consistent mid-range performance&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Amitabh Bachchan:&lt;/strong&gt; Sustained appeal over time&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;div class="insight-box"&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Key Insight:&lt;/strong&gt; While established actors attract viewers, movie ratings vary significantly based on plot, direction, and audience expectations — not just star power.
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-tags"&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;ggplot2&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;dplyr&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;tidyverse&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Statistical Analysis&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-footer"&gt;
        &lt;a href="https://github.com/TasnimAra-Project/Bollywood_Movie_Analysis" class="btn-project"&gt;View on GitHub →&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;span class="impact-badge"&gt;⭐ Personal Passion Project&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;!-- PROJECT 2: Climate Change Shiny App --&gt;
  &lt;div class="project-card"&gt;
    &lt;div class="project-card-inner"&gt;
      &lt;div class="project-meta"&gt;
        &lt;span class="project-category"&gt;Interactive Dashboard & Analysis&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;h3 class="project-title"&gt;Climate Change Shiny App: Challenging Assumptions with Data&lt;/h3&gt;
      &lt;p class="project-highlight"&gt;Growing up in Bangladesh, I always heard about pollution in South Asian countries. I wanted to challenge these assumptions by building an interactive tool to explore global CO₂ emissions data.&lt;/p&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;What I Set Out to Explore&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;Are South Asian countries really the biggest CO₂ contributors?&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;How do emissions compare between developing and developed nations?&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;What are the economic and agricultural impacts of emissions?&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;Key Discoveries&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Challenged Stereotypes:&lt;/strong&gt; South Asian countries aren't the biggest CO₂ contributors&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Comparison:&lt;/strong&gt; Developed nations often have higher per-capita emissions&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-dimensional Impact:&lt;/strong&gt; Economic & agricultural effects across different countries&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;div class="insight-box"&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Technical Achievement:&lt;/strong&gt; Built an interactive Shiny dashboard that allows users to explore emissions data, compare countries, and understand the economic and agricultural consequences of climate change.
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-tags"&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;R Shiny&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;ggplot2&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;dplyr&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;tidyverse&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Comparative Analysis&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-footer"&gt;
        &lt;a href="https://github.com/TasnimAra-Project/Climate_Change_Shiny_App" class="btn-project"&gt;View on GitHub →&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;span class="impact-badge"&gt;🌍 Challenged Assumptions&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;!-- PROJECT 3: Sentiment Analysis --&gt;
  &lt;div class="project-card"&gt;
    &lt;div class="project-card-inner"&gt;
      &lt;div class="project-meta"&gt;
        &lt;span class="project-category"&gt;Natural Language Processing & Business Intelligence&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;h3 class="project-title"&gt;Employee Sentiment Analysis: My Journey with Hugging Face & NLP&lt;/h3&gt;
      &lt;p class="project-highlight"&gt;My first deep dive into Hugging Face and advanced NLP. This project challenged me to work with unlabeled data and find the right sentiment analysis solution for employee communications.&lt;/p&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;The Challenge&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;Unlabeled dataset of employee emails and communications&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;First time working with Hugging Face and advanced NLP models&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;Need to classify sentiment as positive, negative, or neutral&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;My Technical Journey&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Approach:&lt;/strong&gt; Tested BERT, TextBlob, and Vader&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research & Testing:&lt;/strong&gt; Explored multiple Hugging Face libraries&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Final Solution:&lt;/strong&gt; Implemented cardiffnlp/twitter-roberta-base-sentiment&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Manually checked results for quality and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;Business Impact Delivered&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Engagement Insights:&lt;/strong&gt; Identified communication patterns and trends&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flight Risk Model:&lt;/strong&gt; Predicted employees at risk of leaving&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Predictive Analytics:&lt;/strong&gt; Forecasted sentiment scores for future planning&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-tags"&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Hugging Face&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Python&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Transformers&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Pandas&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Scikit-learn&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Matplotlib&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-footer"&gt;
        &lt;a href="https://github.com/TasnimAra-Project/sentiment_analysis_employee" class="btn-project"&gt;View on GitHub →&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;span class="impact-badge"&gt;💬 NLP & Business Intelligence&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;!-- PROJECT 4: Deal Activity Prediction --&gt;
  &lt;div class="project-card"&gt;
    &lt;div class="project-card-inner"&gt;
      &lt;div class="project-meta"&gt;
        &lt;span class="project-category"&gt;Machine Learning & Business Intelligence&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;h3 class="project-title"&gt;Deal Activity Prediction: From Unsupervised to GPT-Enhanced ML&lt;/h3&gt;
      &lt;p class="project-highlight"&gt;My biggest challenge yet: predicting deal closure probability from an unlabeled dataset of wealth management activities. This project pushed me to innovate with GPT-4 labeling and advanced ML techniques.&lt;/p&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;Phase 1: Unsupervised Learning&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KMeans Clustering:&lt;/strong&gt; Extracted numeric features (total activities, engagement days) — 29.8% agreement&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agglomerative Clustering:&lt;/strong&gt; Hierarchical clustering with k=3 — 34.2% agreement&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;Phase 2: GPT-4 Enhanced Supervised Learning&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Processing:&lt;/strong&gt; Flattened nested JSON, created chronological summaries&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GPT-4 Labeling:&lt;/strong&gt; Generated High/Medium/Low labels with reasoning&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model Training:&lt;/strong&gt; Random Forest vs XGBoost with SMOTE balancing&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;div class="insight-box"&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Key Breakthrough:&lt;/strong&gt; GPT-4 labeling captured business context that pure statistical methods missed — a 97% improvement in accuracy (34% → 67% with XGBoost).
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-tags"&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Python&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;OpenAI GPT-4&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;XGBoost&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Random Forest&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Clustering&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Feature Engineering&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-footer"&gt;
        &lt;a href="https://github.com/TasnimAra-Project/Deal-Activity-Prediction" class="btn-project"&gt;View on GitHub →&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;span class="impact-badge"&gt;📈 97% Accuracy Improvement&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;!-- PROJECT 5: Legal Chatbot --&gt;
  &lt;div class="project-card"&gt;
    &lt;div class="project-card-inner"&gt;
      &lt;div class="project-meta"&gt;
        &lt;span class="project-category"&gt;AI Chatbot & Database Design&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;h3 class="project-title"&gt;Social Justice Legal Resource Chatbot: Technology for Community Empowerment&lt;/h3&gt;
      &lt;p class="project-highlight"&gt;My most meaningful project yet: building a chatbot that acts as a virtual social justice lawyer, connecting vulnerable communities with critical legal resources based on their location and specific needs.&lt;/p&gt;

      &lt;h4&gt;Technical Architecture&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SQL Database:&lt;/strong&gt; Comprehensive legal resource repository with location-based indexing&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource Categories:&lt;/strong&gt; Housing, employment, immigration, family law, civil rights&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Geographic Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; ZIP code-based resource matching and filtering&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ChatGPT Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Natural language understanding and context-aware responses&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;

      &lt;div class="insight-box"&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Example Impact:&lt;/strong&gt; "I'm getting kicked out of my home" + ZIP code → immediate housing legal aid resources with contact information, service areas, and eligibility criteria.
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-tags"&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;ChatGPT API&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;SQL&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Python&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;Database Design&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="ptag"&gt;NLP&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;div class="project-footer"&gt;
        &lt;span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-dim); font-style: italic;"&gt;🚧 GitHub repository coming soon&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="impact-badge"&gt;⚖️ Social Impact Project&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

